flowchart TB
accTitle: Planner routing, candidate evaluation, and execution authorization are separate
accDescr: Planner routing selects a search strategy. Candidate evaluation replays a path, checks constraints, and scores feasibility. Candidate selection carries a proposal forward. Execution authorization and dispatch remain downstream; an approval-required flag is not itself permission.

    ROUTE[Planner-method routing] --> PLAN[Planner strategy]
    PLAN --> CAND[Candidate path]
    CAND --> EVAL[Replay and evaluate]
    EVAL --> FEAS{Feasible?}
    FEAS -->|No| REJECT[Reject candidate]
    FEAS -->|Yes| SELECT[Candidate selection]
    SELECT --> FLAG[Approval requirement<br/>may be true]
    FLAG --> AUTH[Downstream authorization<br/>and dispatch]
    AUTH --> EXEC[Grounding execution]
